---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Starfield from "../components/Starfield.astro";
import "../css/reset.css";
import "../css/global.css";
import "../css/index.css";
import Navigation from "../components/Navigation.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Kevin is a software engineer with 10+ years of experience specializing in TypeScript monorepos and PostgreSQL. He founded Starburst Digital in Charlotte, NC to bring enterprise-quality web development and technical consulting to teams that need it most."
    />
    <meta property="og:title" content="About Kevin - Starburst Digital" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="Kevin is a software engineer with 10+ years of experience specializing in TypeScript monorepos and PostgreSQL. He founded Starburst Digital in Charlotte, NC to bring enterprise-quality development to teams that need it most."
    />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="About Kevin - Starburst Digital" />
    <meta
      name="twitter:description"
      content="Kevin is a software engineer with 10+ years of experience specializing in TypeScript monorepos and PostgreSQL. Founded Starburst Digital in Charlotte, NC."
    />
    <title>About - Starburst Digital</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <Starfield>
      <header class="flow">
        <p class="wrapper mt-m-l">
          <a href="/" class="big-brand">Starburst Digital</a>
        </p>
        <Navigation />
      </header>
      <div class="section__inner">
        <div class="wrapper flow region">
          <h1>About Me</h1>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Starfield>

    <main>
      <article class="flow region wrapper">
        <div class="grid" data-layout="50-50">
          <div>
            <img
              src="https://placehold.co/600x800"
              alt="Kevin, founder of Starburst Digital"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="flow">
            <p>
              I'm Kevin, a software engineer based in Charlotte, NC who's been
              building web applications for over a decade. I've worked on
              everything from mission-critical systems for first responders to
              real estate platforms and marketing tools.
            </p>
            <p>
              After years of working with enterprise clients, I realized that
              small businesses were getting a raw deal. Most developers either
              charge enterprise prices or use cookie-cutter templates that don't
              actually solve problems.
            </p>
            <p>
              That's why I started Starburst Digital. I wanted to bring the same
              level of craftsmanship I apply to enterprise work to
              <a href="/services/small-business"
                >small businesses who need it most</a
              >
              — without the enterprise price tag.
            </p>
            <p>
              When you work with me, you're getting a real engineer who
              understands performance, accessibility, and modern web standards.
              Not someone slapping together a WordPress theme or deploying
              generic templates.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <Starfield top static>
        <div class="section__inner">
          <article class="flow region wrapper">
            <h2>What I Believe</h2>
            <p>
              The web should be fast — that's why every site I build is
              optimized to load in under a second. It should be accessible and
              owned by the people who create content for it. You shouldn't need
              to be locked into a platform or pay exorbitant fees just to have a
              professional online presence.
            </p>
            <p>
              Good software is thoughtful software. It's built with real
              understanding of how people use it, not just copy-pasted from
              tutorials or generated by AI without human oversight. That's the
              standard I bring to every
              <a href="/services/small-business">small business website</a> and
              <a href="/services/consulting">consulting engagement</a>.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </Starfield>

      <article class="flow region wrapper">
        <h2>Technical Expertise</h2>
        <div class="grid" data-layout="50-50">
          <div class="card flow">
            <h3>TypeScript & Monorepos</h3>
            <p>
              Large TypeScript codebases are my home turf. I've spent years
              working in and designing monorepos — the tooling, the tradeoffs,
              and the patterns that make them work for big teams. Turborepo, Nx,
              pnpm workspaces, TypeScript project references — I know where
              these tools shine and where they break down.
            </p>
            <p>
              If you're a team struggling with slow builds, tangled
              dependencies, or a repo structure that's grown past what anyone
              planned for, I can help you untangle it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card flow">
            <h3>PostgreSQL</h3>
            <p>
              PostgreSQL is one of the most powerful databases available — and
              one of the most commonly misused. I've worked extensively with
              schema design, query optimization, indexing strategy, and
              migration planning across projects at various scales.
            </p>
            <p>
              When a database starts causing problems — slow queries, connection
              pool exhaustion, schema debt — I know how to diagnose the root
              cause and fix it without a complete rewrite.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="flow region wrapper">
        <h2>Let's Work Together</h2>
        <p>
          If you're a small business owner who wants a real website built by a
          real developer, I'd love to hear from you.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/contact">Get a Free Quote</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
